WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.868
-Welcome back.
I'm here with Ana de Armas.

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:06.501
She stars as Marilyn Monroe in
the Netflix movie "Blonde,"

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:08.334
and we're about to test
our film knowledge

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:10.934
in a new game we call
"Three-Word Movie."

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:11.834
Here we go.

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:15.534
-♪ Three-word movie ♪

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:17.234
-Alright. Here's how it works.

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:19.734
We're going to pick a card with
a name of a movie title on it

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:21.934
and we have to get the other
person to guess the title

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:24.067
using only three words as clues.

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.567
The clues cannot be the name of
anyone in the movie

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:28.634
or the director or any word
in the title.

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:29.901
-Okay.
-Ready for this?

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:32.033
-Mm-hmm.
-Yeah.

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:33.868
What happ-- We played a game
last time you were here, yeah?

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:35.767
-Yeah. You won.

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:38.167
Very, very upset about that.

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:40.000
-I didn't even remember.
No big deal.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.334
We'll be right back.
No, I'm just kidding.

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:42.901
Here we go.

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:43.934
Well, actually,
why don't you go first?

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:45.100
You're my guest.
-You want me to go first?

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.667
-Yeah. You go.
You pick the card.

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.934
And then you -- I won't see it.
But give me three clues

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:51.400
and I'll see if I can guess it.
-Hmm.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.000
This one is very tempting
because --

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.634 --> 00:01:00.167
But that would be a bad word.

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:01.300
So...

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:04.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:06.601
-You want to say it, you can say
it if you want to.

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:08.167
-Let's just say "cat."

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.367
-Okay.

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:11.567
-What would be
a bad word for "cat"?

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.501
-Okay.

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:14.701
-I don't know.

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:16.501
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:18.367
-Shoes.

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:19.267
-Uh-huh.

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:21.968
-Ogre.

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:25.334
-Ogre, cat, shoes?

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.634
Well, but -- Yeah, but --

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:30.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:32.300
"Puss in Boots."

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.400
[ Ding! ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.133
I got it? I got it.

00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:38.934
It took me a while.
I'm slow, but I get it.

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:40.300
Okay. Here we go.
Alright, here we go.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.467
-You got it. Okay.
-Well done.

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.200
-Oh, gosh.
-Okay.

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:50.934
-This is horrible.

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:52.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:54.968
Ugh!

00:01:57.968 --> 00:01:59.334
-Speed!

00:01:59.334 --> 00:02:02.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.567
Flying!

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:06.400
-Um, don't say it again.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.467
-Sorry.

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:11.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:12.801
-It has to be "Top Gun."

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:14.234
-Yes, exactly.
[ Ding! ]

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:17.167
-Yes!

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.767
Why did you say "speed" so much?

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:25.067
-'Cause I wanted to really
channel my Tom Cruise.

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:27.467
I was, like, trying to give
that energy that he does.

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:29.000
He's unbelievable.
Alright. Your turn now.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.200
But here's the deal.
-Oh.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.734
-Round two, this round is
a little harder

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:35.033
because now we can only use two
clues, so the game has changed.

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:37.467
It's now "Two-Word Movie."

00:02:37.467 --> 00:02:39.567
This has never happened before.
We're playing a brand-new game.

00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:40.934
This is "Two-Word Movie."

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:42.534
-You didn't think of
the name before.

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:45.901
-No. We keep changing the --
Yeah. So, this is it.

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:48.801
We're playing the game
"Two-Word Movie."

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.400
-Oh, I love this movie.

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:56.234
Okay.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.100
Travel.

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:04.567
Ah.

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:07.601
DeLorean.

00:03:07.601 --> 00:03:09.434
[ Audience ahhs ]

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:10.634
That was too easy.

00:03:10.634 --> 00:03:11.934
-No. I like that!

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:13.033
"Back to the Future"!

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:14.334
-Yes!
[ Ding! ]

00:03:14.334 --> 00:03:16.000
That was too easy.
-That's not too easy.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.133
It's fine.

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:18.334
I like that.

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:20.267
-I really don't know
who's winning.

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:22.701
-Yeah, I'm not sure
who wins this game.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.567
-Okay.

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:26.000
-Two words?

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.434
I don't need two words.

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:31.634
-Oh. I do.

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:32.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.534 --> 00:03:33.801
-Ready?

00:03:35.501 --> 00:03:36.634
[ as Elvis ] Music.

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:39.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:42.400
-Yes, you don't.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.767
-[ Normal voice ]
One word, right? Here we go.

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:46.801
Just say it.

00:03:46.801 --> 00:03:48.133
-"Elvis."
[ Ding! ]

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:51.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.767
-I love that too.
-Yeah.

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:53.834
-Alright. Final round.

00:03:53.834 --> 00:03:55.801
This round we can only
use one word.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:58.701
It's a game we call
"One-Word Movie."

00:03:58.701 --> 00:04:02.534
-So for this one, you have zero
because you do one word now.

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:04.133
-Yes. Exactly, yeah. Okay.

00:04:04.133 --> 00:04:06.367
-Oh, I love this movie.

00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:09.067
I love my movies.
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:10.501
-One word.

00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:17.334
-If you don't understand
because of my accent,

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:19.033
you missed your chance.
-Okay.

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:20.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:21.934
One word with an accent.

00:04:23.434 --> 00:04:25.033
-Redrum.

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:26.501
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:27.868
-"The Shining"?
-Yes!

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.267
[ Ding! ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:31.834
-I'm not even going to go.
I'm not even going to go.

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:34.534
Ana de Armas!
That's incredible.

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:35.567
That's how you do it. Redrum.

00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:37.200
-Yes.
-Redrum.

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:40.400
Thank you to Ana de Armas.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.501
"Blonde" is available now
on Netflix.

00:04:42.501 --> 00:04:44.133
We'll be right back with
Luke Grimes.

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:45.133
Redrum, right?

